  "id": "ua-pulaski-technical-college-aas-occupational-therapy-assistant",
  "major": "Occupational Therapy Assistant",
  "notes": "PARTNERSHIP: two-year program offered in partnership with Baptist Health College Little Rock (BHCLR). Accredited by the Accreditation Council for Occupational Therapy Education (ACOTE) of the American Occupational Therapy Association (AOTA). Admission: application deadline March 1, file completion deadline March 15; apply to both UA-Pulaski Tech and the OTA program at BHCLR; official high school and college transcripts plus ACT score of 20 or higher (21 or above preferred) sent to BHCLR; prerequisite courses completed with a C or better by the end of the spring semester in the year of application; GPA of 2.7 or above on required prerequisite courses preferred. Some courses have required prerequisites. OTAP courses are only offered as day classes. A drug screen and background check are required of all selected students. Special program fees apply. All Level II fieldwork experiences must be completed within 18 months of the instructional coursework and prior to applying for the national certification exam. Additional prerequisite courses may be required if minimum placement test scores are not met.",
